{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261005_112926_3ece21", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Only the abstract-level report of all-three-TATA edits in one single-cell-derived clone. I did not recover a named genomic copy-number assay or documentation of independent edited clones/donors.\n\nThe abstract’s Methods describes an index patient and one patient-derived iPSC clone with −2, −2 and −17 bp P1 TATA deletions. Its Results mentions qPCR confirming reduced PMP22 expression in mature primary human Schwann cells—not genomic copy-number measurement. “All three” remains the authors’ claim, not independently verified copy number or allele phasing.\n\nExact existing locators, available in the shared library:\n\n1. Source blob:\n   c372e881d67f254c378e879bacfae21260721d6f85eac253e7e1d0aec7cb77f2\n\n   File: primary/pmp22-cis-nascent-search.json\n   Selector: resultList.result where id == \"42801440\"; abstractText → Methods and Results.\n\n2. Receipt-aggregate blob:\n   aa6072954c698015990c69afbcc3a92b41370eaff361c2b745ca1898d407491c\n\n   Select relative_path:\n   primary/pmp22-cis-nascent-search.json.receipt.json\n   primary/PMID42801440-publisher.html.receipt.json\n\n   Read each entry’s original_text. The Europe PMC JSON retrieval succeeded on October 5, 2026, at 18:43:37 UTC. The publisher request at 18:44:53 UTC returned HTTP 200 but only a 3,038-byte “Client Challenge” page; payload_valid is false.\n\nI rechecked the saved payload/receipt hashes and synced the distinction to LABBOOK. No new retrieval or scientific processing was performed. This limits what my retrieval establishes; it does not establish that the full paper lacks a copy-number assay.", "tokens": {"input": 27656, "output": 4180, "total": 1587548, "cache_read": 1555712, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 152643, "timestamp": 1791228423538}
